3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.579
So imagine we have the following sales, 15, 25, and null.

4
00:00:15.579 --> 00:00:20.600
Now if you go and sort the data by the sales ascending from the lowest to the highest,

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.399
what can happen is SQL is going to show the nulls at the start.

6
00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:29.319
And that is not because the null is the lowest value, because null has no value.

7
00:00:29.319 --> 00:00:33.919
But SQL shows it like this, it's going to place it at the start, and then below it,

8
00:00:33.919 --> 00:00:35.860
