9
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.119
So it is 15, and at the end, we're going to have the 25.

10
00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:43.360
Now if you are doing the exact opposite, where you are sorting the data from the highest

11
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.360
to the lowest using descending, so what can happen is SQL is going to sort it like this,

12
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.180
we're going to have 25, then 15.

13
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.500
And the last thing that can appear in the list is going to be the null.

14
00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:00.040
So here SQL is showing the nulls at the end, and that is again, not because nulls are the

15
00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.699
lowest value, it has no value, but SQL do it like this, show it at the end.

16
00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:08.599
So this is how SQL deals with the nulls if you are sorting the data.

